# Stack

- Next.js https://nextjs.org/docs
- Tip Tap for wysiwig https://tiptap.dev/docs
- UI components library Radix UI https://www.radix-ui.com/themes/docs/overview/getting-started


# Requirements

Small lightweight headless CRUD admin panel for https://github.com/pa7lux/giorgobistve repository with Wy

## Fuctionality

1. User authorizes with GitHub App
2. System chacks if user is in https://github.com/pa7lux/giorgobistve contributors list using GitHub API
	2.1 If user is not a contributor — Show component "Contact the admin"
	2.2 If user is contributor, show the admin panel
3. Admin panel should fetch the articles from https://github.com/pa7lux/giorgobistve/tree/master/public/lyrics and provide the ability to make CRUD operations on this files in this directory
4. If user creates new file with admin panel, system automatically updates public/lyrics/index.json with. It adds a new object into the songs array in the file. Example format for object (alilo is a song name):
{
  "id": "alilo",
  "title": "ალილო",
  "titleLatin": "Alilo",
  "description": "Traditional Georgian Christmas carol",
  "file": "alilo.md"
},
5. If user delete a file from the folder, system updates public/lyrics/index.json it searches for the object with the filePath "file": "alilo.md" of deleted file and removes this object from the array
6. All edits and update operations should use WYSIWIG mode or pure markdown mode. User can select this mode.
7. After any of CRUD operations were made in UI, user should press "Publish" button
8. After the "Publish" pressed the system make a push operation to the master branch of the repository
9. Keep the App simple. Build only the functionality we really need in admin panel




